## Description
The compilation error occurs in the INFO macro with some type from std namespace. It seems that operator << overload for std::ostream doesn't work properly for a types from std namespace in the INFO macro.

### Steps to reproduce
```
#define CATCH_CONFIG_MAIN
#include "catch.hpp"
#include <chrono>

using SomeStdType = std::chrono::system_clock::time_point;

std::ostream& operator << ( std::ostream& os, SomeStdType const& std_value )
{
    os << "std type convertion"; // << std_value
    return os;
}

TEST_CASE( "INFO of SomeStdType" )
{
    SomeStdType std_value;
    INFO( "std_value = " << std_value );
    CHECK( std_value == SomeStdType() );
}
```
```
catch.hpp:1970: error: no match for 'operator<<' (operand types are 'std::ostringstream {aka std::__cxx11::basic_ostringstream<char>}' and 'const std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::_V2::system_clock, std::chrono::duration<long long int, std::ratio<1ll, 1000000000ll> > >')
             m_stream << value;
             ~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~
```

### Extra information
* Catch version: **v1.8.2**
* Operating System: **Windows 7 x64**
* Compiler+version: **mingw 5.3.0 32bit, mingw 6.3.0 32bit, msvc 2015 32bit**
